  "details": "I use looks very infrequently, mostly as a \"look this is silly\" for a few minutes and then go back to my usual avatars, however the \"Looks\" section in the action menu is always there, and further lists looks from other avatars than the one I'm wearing, there is hardly a time in which I'd prefer to switch an avatar via that menu, the menu itself reorders based on the most recently selected looks (why?), and I've accidentally clicked the menu many times by now and fear that instead of accessing my current avatar's features I might accidentally switch from an optimized to an unoptimized avatar.\n\nHere are several ways to address my issues with the current implementation:\n\n1. Make the order of \"Looks\" fixed.\n\n2. Move the \"Looks\" section to be nested in \"Quick Actions\".\n\n3. Only present \"Looks\" of the current avatar.\n\n4. With \"Looks\" becoming contextual with the point above, the last selected look could be remembered, like every other avatar feature.",
